{
  "name": "DecideFast — Offline Decision Agent",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## DecideFast — Offline Decision Agent\n\n**What it does:** POST `{\"complaint\": \"...\"}` → local fine-tuned Kev 0.8B (MLX) scores *brakes* probability → AUTO_NO (≤ 0.01), AUTO_YES (≥ 0.99) or HUMAN_REVIEW (in between, never auto-approved).\n\n**Change the model endpoint:** edit only the **Config** node (`kev_endpoint`, thresholds, timeout). No other node needs changing.\n- Same Mac, n8n via npx/npm: `http://127.0.0.1:8010/v1/systemone`\n- n8n in Docker: `http://host.docker.internal:8010/v1/systemone`\n- n8n Cloud cannot reach localhost — use a tunnel URL or run n8n locally.\n\n**Export:** editor menu (⋯, top right) → *Download* → saves the workflow JSON.\n**Run locally:**\n1. Start the Kev MLX server on port 8010.\n2. `npx n8n` (or Docker), open http://localhost:5678.\n3. *Create workflow* → ⋯ → *Import from File* → pick the JSON (or `n8n import:workflow --input=decidefast.json`).\n4. Publish it, then:\n`curl -X POST http://localhost:5678/webhook/decidefast-offline-decision -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"complaint\":\"Brake pedal went to the floor\"}'`\n(Use /webhook-test/ while listening in the editor.)\n\n**Privacy:** successful production runs are not saved (workflow settings); failed runs are saved for debugging — switch to *Do not save* if needed. Responses never echo the complaint.\n\n**Audit trail (local Data Table `decidefast_review_audit`):** every HUMAN_REVIEW case gets a row (PENDING) when the 202 is sent, then is updated with HUMAN_YES / HUMAN_NO / ESCALATED or UNREVIEWED_EXPIRED. No complaint text or reviewer notes are stored; `auto_approved` is always false and `human_confirmed` is true only for a real YES/NO review.\nOptional input: `complaint_id` (else `req-<execution id>`).\nOn a fresh local n8n create the table first (Overview → Data tables) with the same name and columns, then import — nodes find it by name.\n**History:** `GET /webhook/decidefast-review-history?status=REVIEWED&complaint_id=...&limit=50` or open the table in the Data tables view.",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "839a4096-b6db-4595-a643-b1827e0e8d13",
      "name": "Setup & Export Notes",
